# JobBeagle — Enterprise Security Constraints

When changing APIs, auth, payments, or storage, enforce all six:

## 1. Rate limiting & anti-Sybil
- `POST /api/analyze` and `POST /api/extension-capture` must rate-limit by IP and/or user id (in-memory Map or Upstash Redis).
- Preserve device-fingerprint Sybil checks for free Lite credits (`lib/profiles.ts`).

## 2. Payment integrity (PayPal)
- Webhook `POST /api/payment/webhook`: verify with PayPal `verify-webhook-signature` (`PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` + transmission headers) **before** mutating credits.
- Idempotency: if the order is already fulfilled → return 200, do not grant twice.

## 3. Data privacy / PII
- Resume PDF/DOCX: prefer in-memory parse. Storage uploads need strict RLS (owner-only) + 30-day purge via `/api/cron/purge-reports`.
- Do not put card numbers / extreme secrets into Gemini prompts.
- Account delete (`/api/account/delete`) must hard-delete profile, reports, and stored resume files (CCPA).

## 4. Secrets & architecture
- No service-role / Gemini / PayPal secret keys in Client Components.
- Keep RLS enabled on `profiles`, `analysis_reports`, and related tables.
- Profile credits / `membership_tier`: never client-writable. Lock via migration `011_lock_profile_credit_mutations.sql` (narrow UPDATE grants + entitlement trigger). Mutations only via `service_role` or SECURITY DEFINER RPCs (`decrement_*`, `increment_profile_credits`) and a verified PayPal webhook.

## 5. Scraping safety
- Extension scrapers: try/catch, delays, graceful degrade to “paste JD manually” — never crash the SW.

## 6. Generated code gate
- Agent/LLM patches are untrusted until `npm run gate:generated` passes (static review of the diff + `npm run test:security`).
- CI job `generated-code-gate` must stay green on `main`.
- Untrusted JD/resume/search text must stay fenced (`lib/prompt-injection-guard.ts`); never concatenate it into `systemInstruction`.

